@title Ultimate Marvel vs Capcom 3 - arcade, into a fight
@game  PCSE00004
@shot-every 100   # shots through the run so a human can assess render quality

# ============================================================================
# WHAT THIS RECIPE DOES
# Boots, clears the title screen, declines the PSN sign-in, takes OFFLINE MODE ->
# ARCADE, accepts the default team (cursor starts on Ryu) and stage, and plays into
# the first fight, pressing cross (light attack) through it.
#
# HOW IT WAS AUTHORED
# - START at 3000 skips the intro movie. Then the timeline HOLDS (`@wait call
#   sceCtrlPeekBufferPositive`) until the title screen reads the pad - f3148 natively, about
#   f4100 on a phone, whose loads take more frames - and every later INPUT line runs late by
#   the hold, so input frames below 3240 are 140 earlier than the screens they hit natively.
#   START answers "press any button"; DOWN + CROSS picks "do not sign in" on the PSN dialog
#   (a CROSS on YES fails offline and re-asks forever - what a frame-timed DOWN did on the
#   phone). `@section`/`@shot` frames are display frames and do not move.
# - Every later menu is a CROSS every 150 frames: the character select takes three
#   (main + two assists), then the stage select, then a fade to white and NOW LOADING.
# - The character select and stage select are the screens the F32F32 matrix-palette
#   seam fixed (2026-09-26b): before it every portrait and card was invisible.
# ============================================================================

0: @section boot
3000: start
3006:
3010: @wait call sceCtrlPeekBufferPositive   # the title screen starts reading the pad (f3148 native, ~f4100 phone)
3100: start
3106:
3260: down
3266:
3320: cross
3326:
3560: cross
3566:
3710: cross
